---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { REPO_ISSUES_URL, REPO_LICENSE_URL } from '../lib/repo';
---

<BaseLayout title="Licenses & attribution" description="How Agentic Atlas is licensed and how it attributes third-party material.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-fog-100)]">Licenses &amp; attribution</h1>
    <div class="prose-atlas prose prose-invert mt-8 max-w-none">
      <h2>Code - Apache License 2.0</h2>
      <p>
        All source code in this repository (the site, components, and the ingestion
        pipeline) is licensed under the <a href={REPO_LICENSE_URL}>Apache License, Version 2.0</a>.
        You may use, modify, and distribute it under those terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Content - CC BY 4.0</h2>
      <p>
        Original written content (articles, comparisons, glossary entries) is licensed under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</a>,
        unless a specific article's frontmatter declares otherwise. You may share and adapt it
        with attribution to Agentic Atlas.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party material</h2>
      <p>
        Agentic Atlas is a <em>reference</em>: articles summarize, analyze, and link to primary
        sources - vendor docs, engineering blogs, papers, and open-source projects. We do not
        republish third-party text or code. All such material remains the property of its authors
        and under its original license and copyright. Where we quote briefly, we do so under fair
        use with attribution.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every article includes a <strong>Sources &amp; attribution</strong> block listing each
        referenced work with its publisher and, where known, its license. Framework catalog entries
        record the upstream project's own code license (e.g. MIT, Apache 2.0) separately from this
        site's license.
      </p>

      <h2>Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Product and company names - LangChain, LangGraph, Anthropic, Claude, AWS, Google, Hugging
        Face, Model Context Protocol, and others - are trademarks of their respective owners.
        Reference here is nominative and does not imply endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections &amp; takedowns</h2>
      <p>
        If an attribution is wrong or you believe material should be removed, open an issue on the
        <a href={REPO_ISSUES_URL}>GitHub repository</a> and it will be addressed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
